  "operative_text": "Sec. 1 (adding G.S. 14-415.1A(b)): {+(b)+} {+Offense. – It is unlawful for any person who is prohibited pursuant to G.S. 14-415.1 from possessing a firearm or a weapon of mass death and destruction to possess a firearm or weapon of mass death and destruction during the commission or attempted commission of a felony under (i) this Chapter or (ii) Article 5 of Chapter 90 of the General Statutes.+}\nSec. 1 (adding G.S. 14-415.1A(c)): {+(c)+} {+Penalty. – Unless the conduct is covered under some other provision of law providing greater punishment, a person who violates subsection (b) of this section is guilty of the following:+} {+(1)+} {+A Class D felony, if the person discharges the firearm or weapon of mass death and destruction during the commission or attempted commission of the felony.+}\nSec. 1 (adding G.S. 14-415.1A(c)(2)-(3)): {+(2)+} {+A Class F felony, if the person brandishes the firearm or weapon of mass death and destruction during the commission or attempted commission of the felony.+} {+(3)+} {+A Class G felony for any other violation of subsection (b) of this section.+}\nSec. 1 (adding G.S. 14-415.1A(d)): {+(d)+} {+Separate Offense. – A violation of subsection (b) of this section is a separate offense from the underlying felony offense, and G.S. 14-415.1, and shall not merge with any other offense.+}\nSec. 2 (amending G.S. 14-415.1(a)): {+ Violation of this section is not a lesser included offense of G.S. 14-415.1A.+}\nSec. 3: SECTION 3. This act becomes effective December 1, 2023, and applies to offenses committed on or after that date."
